        position: "**A leading Indian maker of large engineered pumps** and, through its subsidiaries, a mid-sized global pump and water-project group with a ₹5,270cr order book.",
        money: "Net cash of about ₹23cr on Screener (₹525cr cash against ₹502cr debt), but operating cash flow has been negative for three years (minus ₹93cr in FY26) as receivables piled up, and management could not give a cash figure on the call. Subsidiaries are only 50-63% owned, so minority partners take a large slice of profit; it plans to buy them out over 2-3 years (for PCI this is contractual), which will need cash. Indian receivables of ₹781cr exceed a year of Indian sales; bills overdue by more than a year rose to about ₹289cr against a provision of only ₹10.6cr, and the company changed how it matches customer payments to bills during FY26. The group auditor relied on other auditors for subsidiaries with about 62% of revenue. A Swiss tax dispute over the Rutschi sale is unresolved. Promoters hold **70.8%**, unchanged over three years.",
